d08a-1bef-5ead-ab02-f3370f825b7b"] ["question-86e2d08a-1bef-5ead-ab02-f3370f825b7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-332746"] ["question-86e2d08a-1bef-5ead-ab02-f3370f825b7b" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}(t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]){e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$"] ["question-86e2d08a-1bef-5ead-ab02-f3370f825b7b" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined."] ["question-86e2d08a-1bef-5ead-ab02-f3370f825b7b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-9383c075-7b49-5325-9b5c-cd8dcad979f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9383c075-7b49-5325-9b5c-cd8dcad979f2"] ["answer-d84b77cd-445d-5e7b-9943-f6360adafe74" :answer/id #uuid "d84b77cd-445d-5e7b-9943-f6360adafe74"] ["answer-d84b77cd-445d-5e7b-9943-f6360adafe74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d84b77cd-445d-5e7b-994